{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LDuUTx4QBknwYEXagHHrkM","type":"tool_result","content":"1:I read the two binding contracts, the arc-outline block, B1's D3.2 entry, and verified every published pointer into Ch 16 by line number against chapters 01–15. **Five of eight sections are pinned by number** (§1–§5); only §6, §7 and §8 are free, and §6 is pinned by topic. Ch 13 also left this stage a direct instruction in an `AUTHOR-REVIEW` comment about frontmatter objectives, which this outline discharges.\n35:#--    authored D2.3 Troubleshooting list and are all deferred to Ch 16 ...\n36:#--    Unless Ch 16's frontmatter carries objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"],\n37:#--    the book's objective index will show a substantial slice of D2.3\n40:#-- Discharged: kb_tags.objectives below carries both. `exam_domain`\n41:#-- stays single-valued and names D3.2, because that is the domain whose\n96:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n102:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n108:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n114:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n120:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n126:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n132:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n138:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n179:  objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n244:The stakes are honest and specific. D3 **doubled** from 8% to 16% in the 2025-11-24 revision [B1], and Debugging is half of it. Legacy prep material sized to the old five-domain blueprint under-serves this domain more than any other. B1's stated posture for D3.2 is blunt — *know which kubectl verb answers which question* — and that is a question a glossary cannot answer, because the verbs are only distinguishable by the question each one is for.\n316:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Troubleshooting Applications — scope), D2.3 (the boundary's far side)\n328:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Init Containers)\n340:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Running Pods; `kubectl debug`), D2.3 (B1 lists `exec` and `debug` under Troubleshooting — see the exam_domain note)\n361:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Services), D2.3\n373:- **Objectives:** D3.2, D2.3\n386:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging StatefulSets)\n399:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (developing and debugging services locally)\n459:| Treating D3.2 Debugging as a different subject from D2.3 Troubleshooting | B1 trap #87. The split is *scope*, not tooling — a question tagged to one may test the other's commands. |\n514:- `kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/debug/debug-application/determine-reason-pod-failure/` — §2, and the D3.2 competency name","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07ea436a-2902-492c-8687-6fe3bb13fd7e","uuid":"31da1558-47f1-4d90-b6cd-d965ac09a2be","timestamp":"2026-08-31T12:56:05.227Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:I read the two binding contracts, the arc-outline block, B1's D3.2 entry, and verified every published pointer into Ch 16 by line number against chapters 01–15. **Five of eight sections are pinned by number** (§1–§5); only §6, §7 and §8 are free, and §6 is pinned by topic. Ch 13 also left this stage a direct instruction in an `AUTHOR-REVIEW` comment about frontmatter objectives, which this outline discharges.\n35:#--    authored D2.3 Troubleshooting list and are all deferred to Ch 16 ...\n36:#--    Unless Ch 16's frontmatter carries objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"],\n37:#--    the book's objective index will show a substantial slice of D2.3\n40:#-- Discharged: kb_tags.objectives below carries both. `exam_domain`\n41:#-- stays single-valued and names D3.2, because that is the domain whose\n96:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n102:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n108:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n114:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n120:    objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n126:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n132:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n138:    objectives: [\"D3.2\"]\n179:  objectives: [\"D3.2\", \"D2.3\"]\n244:The stakes are honest and specific. D3 **doubled** from 8% to 16% in the 2025-11-24 revision [B1], and Debugging is half of it. Legacy prep material sized to the old five-domain blueprint under-serves this domain more than any other. B1's stated posture for D3.2 is blunt — *know which kubectl verb answers which question* — and that is a question a glossary cannot answer, because the verbs are only distinguishable by the question each one is for.\n316:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Troubleshooting Applications — scope), D2.3 (the boundary's far side)\n328:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Init Containers)\n340:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Running Pods; `kubectl debug`), D2.3 (B1 lists `exec` and `debug` under Troubleshooting — see the exam_domain note)\n361:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging Services), D2.3\n373:- **Objectives:** D3.2, D2.3\n386:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (Debugging StatefulSets)\n399:- **Objectives:** D3.2 (developing and debugging services locally)\n459:| Treating D3.2 Debugging as a different subject from D2.3 Troubleshooting | B1 trap #87. The split is *scope*, not tooling — a question tagged to one may test the other's commands. |\n514:- `kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/debug/debug-application/determine-reason-pod-failure/` — §2, and the D3.2 competency name","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
