{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoLQGDWaTHy9PFqgpf3YL9","type":"tool_result","content":"60\t  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `Default`.\n61\t- **Seccomp** — disallow unconfined profiles.\n62\t  Fields: `spec.securityContext.seccompProfile.type` and variants.\n63\t  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `RuntimeDefault`, `Localhost`.\n64\t- **Sysctls** — allow only safe, namespaced sysctls.\n65\t  Fields: `spec.securityContext.sysctls[*].name`.\n66\t  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `kernel.shm_rmid_forced`, `net.ipv4.ip_local_port_range`, `net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start`, `net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies`, `net.ipv4.ping_group_range`, `net.ipv4.ip_local_reserved_ports` (v1.27+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_time` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_fin_timeout` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_intvl` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_probes` (v1.29+).\n67\t\n68\t## Restricted\n69\t\n70\t\"The _Restricted_ policy is aimed at enforcing current Pod hardening best practices, at the expense of some compatibility.\" Targeted at operators and developers of security-critical applications, and at lower-trust users.\n71\t\n72\tThe Restricted policy is cumulative: it includes every Baseline requirement, plus the following.\n73\t\n74\t- **Volume Types** — limit to the safe volume types.\n75\t  Fields: `spec.volumes[*]`.\n76\t  Allowed: `configMap`, `csi`, `downwardAPI`, `emptyDir`, `ephemeral`, `persistentVolumeClaim`, `projected`, `secret`.\n77\t- **Privilege Escalation** (v1.8+) — prevent setuid/setgid escalation.\n78\t  Fields: `spec.containers[*].securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation` and variants.\n79\t  Allowed: `false`. (Linux only, v1.25+.)\n80\t- **Running as Non-root** — require non-root execution.\n81\t  Fields: `spec.securityContext.runAsNonRoot` and the container/init/ephemeral variants.\n82\t  Allowed: `true`.\n83\t- **Running as Non-root user** (v1.23+) — forbid UID 0.\n84\t  Fields: `spec.securityContext.runAsUser` and variants.\n85\t  Allowed: any non-zero value, or `undefined/null`.\n86\t- **Seccomp** (v1.19+) — mandate explicit confinement.\n87\t  Fields: `spec.securityContext.seccompProfile.type` and variants.\n88\t  Allowed: `RuntimeDefault`, `Localhost`. (Linux only, v1.25+.)\n89\t- **Capabilities** (v1.22+) — drop all, and optionally add back only `NET_BIND_SERVICE`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07ea436a-2902-492c-8687-6fe3bb13fd7e","uuid":"bb3dc84f-b48e-481e-be59-a518dfa603ee","timestamp":"2026-08-31T13:00:16.634Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/k8s-docs-pod-security-standards-profiles-2026-08-31.md","content":"  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `Default`.\n- **Seccomp** — disallow unconfined profiles.\n  Fields: `spec.securityContext.seccompProfile.type` and variants.\n  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `RuntimeDefault`, `Localhost`.\n- **Sysctls** — allow only safe, namespaced sysctls.\n  Fields: `spec.securityContext.sysctls[*].name`.\n  Allowed: `undefined/nil`, `kernel.shm_rmid_forced`, `net.ipv4.ip_local_port_range`, `net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start`, `net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies`, `net.ipv4.ping_group_range`, `net.ipv4.ip_local_reserved_ports` (v1.27+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_time` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_fin_timeout` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_intvl` (v1.29+), `net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_probes` (v1.29+).\n\n## Restricted\n\n\"The _Restricted_ policy is aimed at enforcing current Pod hardening best practices, at the expense of some compatibility.\" Targeted at operators and developers of security-critical applications, and at lower-trust users.\n\nThe Restricted policy is cumulative: it includes every Baseline requirement, plus the following.\n\n- **Volume Types** — limit to the safe volume types.\n  Fields: `spec.volumes[*]`.\n  Allowed: `configMap`, `csi`, `downwardAPI`, `emptyDir`, `ephemeral`, `persistentVolumeClaim`, `projected`, `secret`.\n- **Privilege Escalation** (v1.8+) — prevent setuid/setgid escalation.\n  Fields: `spec.containers[*].securityContext.allowPrivilegeEscalation` and variants.\n  Allowed: `false`. (Linux only, v1.25+.)\n- **Running as Non-root** — require non-root execution.\n  Fields: `spec.securityContext.runAsNonRoot` and the container/init/ephemeral variants.\n  Allowed: `true`.\n- **Running as Non-root user** (v1.23+) — forbid UID 0.\n  Fields: `spec.securityContext.runAsUser` and variants.\n  Allowed: any non-zero value, or `undefined/null`.\n- **Seccomp** (v1.19+) — mandate explicit confinement.\n  Fields: `spec.securityContext.seccompProfile.type` and variants.\n  Allowed: `RuntimeDefault`, `Localhost`. (Linux only, v1.25+.)\n- **Capabilities** (v1.22+) — drop all, and optionally add back only `NET_BIND_SERVICE`.","numLines":30,"startLine":60,"totalLines":102}}}
